<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<subsection xml:id="sec-14-honors-projects-and-research-long">
  <title>Honors Projects &amp; Research</title>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Research</title>
    <p>
      Midland College offers undergraduate research opportunities in mathematics,
      including mathematical modeling projects that address real-world problems.
      Students can begin with guided practice projects and later develop original
      projects connected to community needs.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Honors Projects</title>
    <p>
      Honors projects typically include written, visual, and oral components.
      Project scope and format are determined with the instructor and may include
      expository work, modeling, historical analysis, or presentation-based outcomes.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <p>
    Students interested in research or an honors project should contact the instructor early
    in the semester to plan timelines and expectations.
  </p>
</subsection>
